                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Fusion category
              %tr
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Finite abelian group
                %td{:style => "text-align: left;"} Braided fusion category
          %h2#SpecialCaseOfZGradedVectorSpaces
            Special case of
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %p
            The case
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi G
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℤ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G = \mathbb{Z}
            serves as a base for many other applications of the same basic idea. It has some of its own ‘traditional’ terminology and structure that links it to
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/differential+object"} differential objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/chain+complex"} chain complex
            of vector spaces. We will use ‘gvs’ as an abbreviation for this sort of graded vector space and ‘dgvs’ for the differential form. (Of course, the theory easily adapts to handle graded modules over a ring, and with some restriction, to graded groups.) Basing algebras on dgvs gives differential graded algebras (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dg-algebra"}> dg-algebra
            ) and so on.
          %h2#concepts Concepts
          %p
            The entry here will be a sort of lexicon of some terms which are taken from a source on
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rational+homotopy+theory"} rational homotopy theory
          %p The lexicon will be spread over a number of entries with links given in the table of contents ion the right hand side at the top.
          %p
            %strong Note
            With
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
          %h3#pregraded_vector_spaces (Pre-)graded vector spaces
          %p
            A
            %em
              pre-
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
              \-graded vector space
            (pre-gvs) is a direct sum
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ∈
                        %mi ℤ
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \bigoplus_{p \in \mathbb{Z}} V_p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_p
            are said to be
            = succeed "." do
              %em
                homogeneous of degree
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \in V_p
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo =
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |x| = p
          %p
            Sometimes it may be convenient to write
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mover
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ¯
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi x
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \bar{x} = (-1)^{|x|}x
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mo +
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo &gt;
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V_+ = \bigoplus_{p \gt 0} V_p
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V^p = V_{-p}
          %p For the purposes of this lexicon:
          %p
            A
            %em graded vector space
            (gvs) is a positively or negatively graded pre-gvs that is either
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 0
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \sum_{p \geq 0} V_p
            or
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∑
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ≤
                        %mn 0
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \sum_{p \leq 0} V^p
            = succeed "-grading" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℕ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{N}
          %p
            We consider the field
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            to be a pre-gvs with
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi k
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mn 0
                    %mo =
                    %mi k
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k)_0 = k
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi k
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi p
                  %mo =
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (k)_p =0
            if
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                    %mo ≠
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p\neq 0
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is of
            %em finite type
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi dim
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo &lt;
                  %mn ∞
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} dim(V_p) \lt \infty
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
          %p
            A linear map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f :V\to W
            between pre-gvs is
            %em
              of degree
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            if
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi q
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊆
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mi q
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(V_q) \subseteq W_{p+q}
            for all
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi q
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} q
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mi q
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊆
                    %msup
                      %mi W
                      %mrow
                        %mi q
                        %mo −
                        %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f(V^q) \subseteq W^{q-p}
          %p
            A
            %em morphism
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : V\to W
            is a linear map of degree zero. Pregraded vector spaces and the morphisms between them define the category
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi pre
                      %mi GVS
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {pre GVS}
          %p
            The set of all linear maps of degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi p
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} p
            from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            will be denoted
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom_p(V,W)
            and we set
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Hom
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mi p
                  %msub
                    %mi Hom
                    %mi p
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                  %mi W
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Hom(V,W) = \bigoplus_p Hom_p(V,W).
          %p
            Of course, we now have two notations for the same object,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mi pre
                      %mi GVS
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi Hom
                      %mn 0
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ,
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {pre GVS}(V,W) = Hom_0(V,W)
          %h3#suspension Suspension
          %p
            If
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r \in \mathbb{Z}
            = succeed "-suspension" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is given by
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mi r
                  %mi V
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mi r
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s^r V)_n = V_{n-r}.
          %p
            We will need
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^{-1}
            in particular. Of course,
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mi V
                    %msub
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi n
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s^{-1}V)_n = V_{n+1}
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mi r
                    %mi V
                    %msup
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mi p
                    %mo =
                    %msup
                      %mi V
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo +
                        %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (s^r V)^p = V^{p+r}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mi r
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mi r
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^r: V \to s^r V
            is an isomorphism of degree
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} -r
            having
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi r
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^{-r}
            as its inverse.
          %p
            Note that the
            = succeed "-suspension" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi r
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} r
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mi r
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^r V
            of a
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is also commonly denoted by
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V[-r]
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mi r
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^{-r} V
            by
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                    %mi r
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V[r]
          %p
            (This is the basic example of the
            %strong suspension functor
            discussed in
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/triangulated+category"} triangulated category
          %h3#duals Duals
          %p
            The dual of a (pre-)gvs
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#V
            defined by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo #
                          %mi V
                          %msub
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mi p
                        %mtd
                          %mo :
                          %mo =
                          %msub
                            %mi Hom
                            %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mi V
                          %mo ,
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                          %mi Vect
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi p
                          %mo ,
                          %mi k
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo ≅
                          %mo #
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msub
                            %mi V
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo #
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %msup
                            %mi V
                            %mi p
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  (\#V)_p &amp;: = Hom_p(V,k)\\
                  \&amp;\cong{Vect}(V_{-p},k)\\
                  \&amp;\cong\#(V_{-p})\\
                  \&amp; =\#(V^p).
                  \\end{aligned}
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f : V\to W
            is of degree
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |f|
            %em transpose
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo
                    %mi t
                  %mi f
                  %mo :
                  %mo #
                  %mi W
                  %mo →
                  %mo #
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^t f : \#W \to \#V
          %p is given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi ψ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mi ψ
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (^t f)(\psi)(x) = (-1)^{|f||\psi|}\psi f(x),
          %p
            for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ψ
                  %mo ∈
                  %mo #
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \psi \in \#W
            and
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi x
                    %mo ∈
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x\in V
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi f
                    %mi W
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mi g
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\stackrel{f}{\to}W\stackrel{g}{\to}X
          %p
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi g
                  %mo ∘
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                  %mi f
                  %mo ∘
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                    %mi t
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ^t (g\circ f)   = (-1)^{|f||g|}(^t f\circ {}^t g).
            } In particular, for
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi f
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f
            an isomorphism
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi t
                  %mi f
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %msup
                    %mo
                    %mi t
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi f
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} ( ^t f)^{-1} = (-1)^{|f|} ^t (f^{-1}).
          %h3#duality Duality
          %p
            Let
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a gvs, by convention in the duality
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo ;
                  %mspace{:width => "1em"}
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                  %mo :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ↔
                  %mo #
                  %mi V
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \langle \quad ; \quad \rangle: V \leftrightarrow \#V,
          %p
            we will usually assume
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is non-negatively graded (so
            = succeed ")," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo =
                    %msub
                      %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                      %mrow
                        %mi p
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 0
                    %msub
                      %mi V
                      %mi p
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V = \bigoplus_{p\geq 0}V_p
          %p
            If
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is of finite type then
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo #
                    %mo #
                    %mi V
                    %mo ≅
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#\#V \cong V
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi s
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo #
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s(\#V)
            can be identified with
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo #
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msup
                    %mi s
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mn 1
                  %mi V
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \#(s^{-1}V)
            and similarly
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo #
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo #
                    %mi s
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s^{-1}(\#V) = \#s(V)
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mtable{:columnalign => "right left right left right left right left right left", :columnspacing => "0em", :displaystyle => "true"}
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %msup
                            %mi s
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi z
                          %mo ;
                          %mi su
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mi z
                          %mo ;
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo ,
                      %mtr
                        %mtd
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mi s
                          %mi z
                          %mo ;
                          %msup
                            %mi s
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                              %mn 1
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                        %mtd
                          %mo =
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                          %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                          %mn 1
                          %msup
                            %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                            %mrow
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mi z
                              %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                              %mo +
                              %mn 1
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟨
                          %mi z
                          %mo ;
                          %mi u
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ⟩
                          %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  \\begin{aligned}
                  \\langle s^{-1}z;su\rangle &amp;= (-1)^{|z|} \langle z;u \rangle,\\
                  \\langle s z;s^{-1}u  \rangle &amp;= (-1)^{|z|+1}\langle z;u \rangle.\end{aligned}
          %p
            This sign convention is needed to ensure that
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi s
                    %msup
                      %mi s
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                        %mn 1
                    %mo =
                    %mi id
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} s s^{-1} = id
          %h3#tensor_products Tensor products
          %p
            The
            %em
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tensor+product"} tensor product
            of two pre-gvs,
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            and
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V\otimes W
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi W
                  %msub
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi n
                  %mo =
                  %munder
                    %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ⨁
                    %mrow
                      %mi p
                      %mo +
                      %mi q
                      %mo =
                      %mi n
                  %msub
                    %mi V
                    %mi p
                  %mo ⊗
                  %msub
                    %mi W
                    %mi q
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (V\otimes W)_n = \bigoplus_{p + q = n}V_p\otimes W_q.
          %p On morphisms
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mn 1
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi g
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                      %mi f
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi v
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⊗
                  %mi g
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi w
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (f\otimes g) (v\otimes w) = (-1)^{|g||f|}(f(v) \otimes g(w))
          %p
            and is of degree
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi f
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mo +
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi g
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} |f| + |g|
          %p
            In particular there is a natural injection
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo #
                    %mi V
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mo #
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo →
                    %mo #
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi V
                    %mo ⊗
                    %mi W
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\#V)\otimes (\#W) \to \#(V\otimes W)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            or
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi W
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} W
            is of finite type.
          %p
            This tensor product makes the category of graded vector spaces into a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/monoidal+category"} monoidal category
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/symmetric+monoidal+category"} symmetric monoidal category
            with
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/braiding"} braiding
            the evident braiding inherited from the underlying vector spaces.
          %p
            Notice that given suitable
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cocycles"} cocycles
            on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi G
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} G
            = succeed "-graded" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi ℤ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{Z}/2
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/super+vector+spaces"} super vector spaces
